  "kind": "event",
  "title": "First Council of Nicaea",
  "summary": "Emperor Constantine brought bishops to Nicaea in 325 to settle the dispute over Arius, who taught that Christ was above humanity but below God. The council issued a creed calling the Son of one substance with the Father, excommunicated Arius and the bishops who would not sign, and dealt with the dating of Easter. Sources disagree on the exact dates and the number of bishops.",
